<</Title(The transient Couette flow was analyzed using explicit FTCS and implicit  numerical schemes and compared with the analytical solution. The velocity profiles show the development of fluid motion between a stationary lower plate and an upper plate moving at a constant velocity. For the explicit scheme with Fo=0.55, the velocity profile exhibits severe oscillations and the relative error increases significantly, indicating numerical instability. In contrast, for Fo=0.45 and Fo=0.25, the explicit solutions remain stable and closely follow the analytical profile. The implicit scheme remains stable for the tested cases, although its error decreases more gradually than that of the stable explicit cases.)/Dest[1266 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1473 0 R>>
